\c 3
\s1 Nebuchadnezzar’s Golden Statue
\p \v 1 \w King|strong="H04430"\w* \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H05020"\w* \w made|strong="H05648"\w* \w a golden|strong="H01722"\w* \w statue|strong="H06755"\w*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft Or \fqa image\ft ; here and throughout Daniel 3\f* \w . . .|strong="H01768"\w* \w sixty|strong="H08361"\w* \w cubits|strong="H00521"\w* \w high|strong="H07314"\w* \w and six|strong="H08353"\w* \w cubits|strong="H00521"\w* \w wide|strong="H06613"\w*,\f + \fr 3:1 \ft The statue was approximately 90 feet high and 9 feet wide (27.4 meters high and 2.7 meters wide).\f* \w and he set it up|strong="H06966"\w* \w on the plain|strong="H01236"\w* \w of Dura|strong="H01757"\w* \w in the province|strong="H04083"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H00895"\w*. \v 2 \w Then King|strong="H04430"\w* \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H05020"\w* \w sent|strong="H07972"\w* \w word to assemble|strong="H03673"\w* \w the satraps|strong="H00324"\w*, \w prefects|strong="H05460"\w*, \w governors|strong="H06347"\w*, \w advisers|strong="H00148"\w*, \w treasurers|strong="H01411"\w*, \w judges|strong="H01884"\w*, \w magistrates|strong="H08614"\w*, \w and all the other|strong="H03606"\w* \w officials|strong="H07984"\w* \w of the provinces|strong="H04083"\w* \w to attend|strong="H00858"\w* \w the dedication|strong="H02597"\w* \w of the statue|strong="H06755"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01768"\w* \w [he]|strong="H04430"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05020"\w* \w had set up|strong="H06966"\w*.
